  ctaTitle="Vector index builds blocking a release, or vector search too slow for production?"
  ctaDescription="A pgvector review measures build time, memory, recall and filtered-query latency on your data and gives you index settings, a build procedure and the numbers to validate them."
>
  <p class="notice"><strong>Short answer:</strong> an HNSW build is fast only while the whole graph fits in <code>maintenance_work_mem</code>. Raise it for the build session to more than the expected index size. If you want parallel workers, check that PostgreSQL will actually start them: for vectors stored in TOAST it often will not, until you set the table's <code>parallel_workers</code> option. In Docker or Kubernetes, give <code>/dev/shm</code> at least as much space as <code>maintenance_work_mem</code>, or the parallel build fails.</p>

  <p>HNSW is the index type most teams pick for pgvector, and its build is the slow part. I built the same index 14 times on pgvector 0.8.7 and PostgreSQL 18.6 in Docker, changing memory, workers and shared memory, to see which settings matter. The scripts and full output are in the <a href="https://github.com/kiransabne04/databasedeveloper.dev/tree/main/labs/pgvector-hnsw-build">lab folder</a>.</p>

  <nav class="notice" aria-label="On this page">
